 "productionNotes": "No exact production total for the EM1 Civic Si could be read for this research, so none is given. Two published figures exist and they agree, but both are round numbers. Hagerty writes that Honda sold more than 640,000 Civics over the 1999 and 2000 model years and that only 30,000 of them were Si coupes, and DrivingLine gives approximately 30,000 EM1s for the two-year run. Hagerty does not vouch for its own count, writing that production numbers are educated guesses at best. The Golden Era Honda site publishes a 1999-2000 Civic Si production table by year and color and says its figures come from Honda's North American VIN database, the one used for recalls, but the table is published as images and its figures could not be read here; that table is the obvious next source for a firm total. The color split rests on one source: Hagerty says 50 percent of Si coupes were painted Electron Blue Pearl, with the other half divided between Flamenco Black Pearl and Milano Red. No source consulted gives a 1999 versus 2000 split. Because 30,000 is an approximation from two journalism sources rather than a factory or registry figure, productionTotal is null rather than 30000. Coverage notes: the US model years, the three colors and the $17,445 launch price come from 1999 launch text published on The Auto Channel and from Honda's own Civic Si timeline. No fueleconomy.gov row for the Si and no NHTSA recall listing were retrieved, so EPA ratings and recall campaigns are not stated from federal sources; the fuel economy figures quoted come from a 1999 road test spec table. Fault and repair-cost coverage (category 5) is thin: one US buyer's guide and theft data from the National Insurance Crime Bureau, with no specialist shop pricing. Category 7 does not apply to this page.",
